<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper A · Learner paper</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/a/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper A</p><h1>Learner paper</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 A</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">志愿活动: volunteer activity</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first help at this school activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上学期刚开学时</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上学期结束时</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 这学期放假以后</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">介绍板: display board</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What had the man expected before his first introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 新同学会先动手做东西</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 新同学都会带材料来</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 新同学会听完长介绍</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why did the second introduction attract more participants?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把原来的介绍讲得更长</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不再回答新同学的问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先让大家体验自己能做什么</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">群消息: group-chat messages</p><p class="gloss">分工: division of tasks</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What need does the woman state?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天八点以前完成所有作业</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 完全不参加小组讨论</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 九点以后不再看群消息</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What is the likely purpose of the man’s proposal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 让大家以后只用电话交流</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 减少一直等消息的负担，同时保留合作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 让不及时回复的人退出小组</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">报名: sign up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do first to prepare for the future activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 这个月马上报名参加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 请弟弟替自己讲故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每周读故事并试着复述</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">校园广播: school radio</p><p class="gloss">摄影: photography</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What preparation is required for Activity A?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 星期五前交自己写的介绍</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周日下午自己带相机</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先买一台新的相机</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits the man’s situation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 直接认定自己已报上甲活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 改去只在周日下午开的乙活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 修改介绍后确认甲活动是否有名额</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">录音: record audio</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for finding the information?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 陈林</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 苏安</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 最后整理的人</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What sequence have they finally agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周二资料，周四录音，周五整理后交</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周三先录音，再等周四的资料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周五交完以后再整理</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">采访: interview</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of this programme?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公布下一次比赛的获奖名单</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 介绍同学从经历中改变做法的故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 教授参加比赛必须使用的方法</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">封面: cover</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Xiaoyu’s view of the notebook change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从只看新旧，变为注意里面记录的经历</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从想买新本子，变为以后都不用新本子</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从喜欢画画，变为只愿意写字</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude is best supported by the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 按具体用途和记忆决定去留</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 旧东西越多就一定越好</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只要封面漂亮就应该留下</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">修补: mend</p><p class="gloss">提手: handle</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What must participants do before the morning activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先交修补工具的钱</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把要修的布袋洗干净</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先把所有旧书整理完</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan fits the man’s availability and goal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 下午参加旧书整理</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 下午才开始修补布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 上午参加布袋修补</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">堆放: pile up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What is the revised collection time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周六上午九点</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周五下午九点</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周六下午原定时间</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">匆忙: hurried</p><p class="gloss">从容: unhurried</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What change does Xiaoning try this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一写完作业就立刻出门</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 睡前半小时不用手机</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每天早上多花半小时找东西</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. What explains her reported change in the morning?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 两周以后不再需要准备书包</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 晚上先放好书包，早上少了找东西</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她保证每天都完全做到计划</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">长跑: distance running</p><p class="gloss">闷着: keep feelings to oneself</p><p class="gloss">名次: placing in a competition</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which suggestion fits the woman’s present circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天练习一小时再决定是否活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 约朋友走十分钟，不以比赛为目标</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等到有完整比赛时间才开始活动</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What does the man’s reflection suggest he now values?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 共同坚持的过程，不只看名次</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只有得到奖才算值得参加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不再愿意和朋友一起活动</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">上学期第一个星期五，学校请我们帮助新同学。我原来以为自己要站在门口讲话，到了才知道，老师让我陪两位同学找实验教室。我先看了楼层图，再带他们上楼。那天下午我说的话不多，却一直在认真听他们的问题。回家后，我把这次第一次帮助别人的经历写进了日记。</p></div><p class="gloss">实验教室: science classroom</p><p class="gloss">楼层图: floor plan</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did the writer help the new students?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上学期最后一个星期五</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上学期第一个星期五</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本学期第一天</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">我参加校刊小组以前，总以为采访就是提前写好问题，再请对方一个个回答。第一次采访门口的保安叔叔时，我把问题问完就准备离开。他笑着问，我要不要听听他最难忘的一天。我这才放下本子，认真听他讲有一次怎样帮助迷路的新生。<br>回到小组，我没有按原来的问题顺序写文章，而是先写那一天发生的事，再补上人物介绍。老师说，读者因此更容易了解他的工作。我发现，准备问题当然有用，但愿意听对方想讲的事情也很重要。下次采访，我还会准备问题，却不会只盯着自己的本子。</p></div><p class="gloss">校刊: school magazine</p><p class="gloss">保安: security guard</p><p class="gloss">新生: new student</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What did the writer originally expect an interview to be?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 完全不用提前准备任何问题</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 由被采访的人替自己写文章</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 按事先写好的问题逐个问答</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why did the writer change the article’s organization?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为老师要求删除所有人物介绍</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为原来没有准备任何采访问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先呈现具体经历，更便于读者理解人物工作</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小组通知：我们要在周四放学前交一份校园生活介绍。周二请每个人提出一个主题，周三中午一起确定内容。资料可以从校园观察中获得，不要求采访校外的人。每个人都要负责一小部分，不能只由一位同学完成。<br>小梅回复：我周三中午要参加合唱练习，不能开会。我愿意整理食堂排队的观察，周二晚上就把笔记发给大家。请你们先讨论；如果主题合适，再告诉我需要补什么。我周四午休还能修改，但放学后不能留下来。</p></div><p class="gloss">合唱: choir</p><p class="gloss">排队: queue</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. By when must the group submit its introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周三中午开会前</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周四放学前</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周四放学以后</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. What is a reasonable next action for the other members?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 等周四放学后再让她开始找资料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周三讨论她的笔记，尽早反馈供她周四午休修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为她不能开会，就认定她不能参与</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">林安想在下学期参加学校的故事分享小组。她喜欢读书，却发现自己讲故事时容易漏掉中间的经过。她给这个月定了一个小目标：每周读完一篇短故事，写下三个先后发生的动作，再试着不看书讲给同伴听。她暂时没有报名，准备月末听听同伴的意见，再决定是否参加。</p></div><p class="gloss">漏掉: leave out</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is Lin’an’s preparation plan for this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每周读故事，记动作顺序，再试着复述</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先报名，再请别人代替自己读书</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只记故事结尾，不再练习讲述</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">下月学校开放两种体验活动。甲是星期六上午的讲解练习，参加者先观察一处校园空间，再在周五前交一份简短介绍。老师提供图片，不需要自己买设备。乙是星期日下午的影像记录，参加者须带能够拍摄的设备，并提前学习一种剪辑工具。两个活动都可以帮助同学整理信息，但练习方式不同。<br>小禾希望以后能把复杂事情讲得更清楚。她只有星期六上午有空，已经记下了图书角的使用情况，却还没有整理成介绍。她不想为了这次活动购买设备。她准备先看清要求，再确认是否还有位置，不会仅因时间合适就当作报名成功。</p></div><p class="gloss">剪辑: video editing</p><p class="gloss">设备: equipment</p><p class="gloss">图书角: classroom reading corner</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which difference between the activities is stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲练习讲解并提供图片，乙要带拍摄设备</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要求购买设备，乙完全不需要准备</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲乙都只在星期日下午进行</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which action best matches Xiaohe’s goal and constraints?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 购买新设备后报名乙，不考虑周日时间</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把观察整理成介绍，再询问甲的名额</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 仅凭甲的时间合适就停止准备</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">活动公告：读书社本周要制作一张共同推荐单。每人选择一个校园生活话题，写出自己的看法和一个具体例子。周三晚上八点前发给负责人，周四中午讨论，再于放学前定稿。推荐单不要求所有人意见相同，但每一项都要说明理由。<br>周宁的回复：我想谈午休时怎样使用图书角。我认为应该留出安静读书的地方，因为上次大家同时讨论时，有同学没法专心。我周四中午有事，不过周三晚上七点能发来内容，也愿意在讨论前补充一个例子。请把讨论后的修改意见发给我，我当天放学前还有时间调整。</p></div><p class="gloss">推荐单: recommendation list</p><p class="gloss">定稿: finalize</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. What reason does Zhou Ning give for a quiet reading space?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 负责人要求所有人意见一样</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 图书角周四中午将不开放</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 讨论声曾影响同学专心读书</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Does Zhou Ning’s proposed contribution fit the stated process?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 可以，七点先交看法和例子，再按讨论意见修改</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不可以，因为公告禁止缺席会议的人交内容</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 可以，但必须等周四讨论结束才第一次交内容</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校园广播本周开设“试过以后”小栏目，不介绍比赛成绩，而请同学讲一次自己改变办法的经历。第一期有人谈怎样从只读书名改成先翻目录，也有人谈怎样把难记的路线画出来。节目最后会请听众选择一种愿意尝试的办法，并写下一周后的感受。栏目并不保证每种办法都适合每个人。</p></div><p class="gloss">栏目: programme segment</p><p class="gloss">目录: table of contents</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What is the main idea of this programme introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分享改变做法的经历，并鼓励有选择地尝试</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 按比赛成绩给全校同学排出名次</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 保证听众使用同一种办法都能成功</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">短故事《不一样的礼物》中，小岚想给朋友做一本相册。她起初只找颜色漂亮的纸，觉得好看就够了。后来她看到朋友保留的一张模糊照片：那是两人第一次一起完成小组任务时拍的。照片并不清楚，朋友却把它放在书桌上。<br>小岚于是把那张照片放在相册第一页，旁边写下当时大家怎样互相帮忙。其他页面仍然用了她喜欢的彩纸，但每页都多了一段小记。朋友说，自己最喜欢的是那些一起经历过的事。故事结尾，朋友把相册放在常看的书架上，翻到第一页，笑着又说起那天的事。小岚看着旁边还没用完的彩纸，决定留着做下一份礼物。</p></div><p class="gloss">相册: photo album</p><p class="gloss">模糊: blurred</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Why does Xiaolan put the unclear photo on the first page?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为朋友只喜欢看不清楚的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 它记录了两人共同完成任务的经历</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为她决定整本相册不再用彩纸</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which interpretation best fits the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 外观之外，共同经历也能让礼物有意义</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有好看的礼物都没有价值</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有模糊照片才值得保存</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">学校准备举行一次旧物再用活动。修补区只接收已经清洗的布袋，工具由老师提供，参加者须先说明哪里需要修补。分享区接收内容完整、适合同龄人阅读的旧书，不收缺页的练习册。两个区域都在周六上午开放，大家可以按自己的需要选择，不必每个区域都去。<br>小齐想让破了一个小口的布袋继续使用，家里的几本书也想带来。她周六只有一个小时，因此决定先把袋子洗好，再检查书页。如果书适合分享，就在修袋前先送到分享区；如果书有缺页，就暂时留下处理，而不是把它交给别人。她最想完成的仍是修好布袋。</p></div><p class="gloss">缺页: missing pages</p><p class="gloss">同龄人: people of the same age</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the sharing area refuse?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 缺页的练习册</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 内容完整且适合同龄人的旧书</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有已经读过的书</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan meets Xiaoqi’s goal and the event’s rules?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不检查书页，把有缺页的书先送走</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 为了每区都参加，放弃自己最想修好的布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先洗袋查书，再按书的状况决定是否分享并修袋</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">“少用一次性杯子”活动只针对本周的读书分享会。学校鼓励同学带自己的杯子，但忘带的人可以借用会场清洗好的杯子，结束后放回指定位置。通知提醒，活动不是要求大家马上扔掉家里所有旧杯子，也不限制正常喝水。负责人希望先从一次活动开始，看看怎样做更方便。</p></div><p class="gloss">一次性: single-use</p><p class="gloss">指定: designated</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which statement correctly describes the initiative’s scope?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 要求全校立刻扔掉所有旧杯子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先在本周分享会试行，忘带杯子可以借</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本周没有自带杯子的人都不能喝水</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小青的两周记录：以前我总在睡前才找第二天要用的东西，有时一边找一边看手机，早上又要确认一次。这两周我试着吃完晚饭就把书包整理好，睡前留十分钟听轻松的音乐。不是每天都按计划做到，不过我把做到和没做到的日子都记了下来。<br>第二周末，我发现自己早上少找了几次作业本，出门时也没有那么急。我愿意再试两周，看看遇到作业多的时候还能不能坚持。朋友建议我直接说“这个办法人人都该用”，我没有这样写：这些只是我的记录，也可能有别的原因影响那几天的感受。我想先继续观察，再决定怎样调整。</p></div><p class="gloss">确认: check/confirm</p><p class="gloss">观察: observe</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoqing explicitly report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从此每天都绝不会再着急</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已经证明这个办法适合所有人</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 早上找作业本的次数少了几次</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does she decide to keep observing?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为两周里她从来没有一次做到计划</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为她已经确定所有变化只由音乐造成</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已有一些变化，但还要看忙碌时是否可坚持</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年参加校园寻路活动时，我一心想让小组最快到达。走错一次后，我一直埋怨自己，差点不想继续。队友没有催我，反而请我画下刚才经过的路口。我们虽然没拿到名次，却一起找到了终点。我后来最常想起的，是大家愿意停下来重新商量的那一刻。<br>最近同学邀请我参加新的小组活动。我每周只有两次放学后的短时间，不可能天天准备。我决定先说明这个限制，问能否负责一小段路线记录。如果大家同意，我就按时完成这部分，再听取反馈。这一次，我把给小组的第一条消息改了三遍，最后写的是自己能完成什么、希望得到什么反馈，而不是先问有没有机会拿第一。</p></div><p class="gloss">埋怨: blame/complain about</p><p class="gloss">反馈: feedback</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which current adjustment is supported by the past experience and present limits?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 承诺每天都能准备，避免提到时间限制</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 说明可用时间，协商一项能完成的路线记录任务</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有保证小组第一名才愿意参加</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What can reasonably be inferred about the writer’s changed view?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要出错，以后就不该参加小组活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要大家一起参加，就不必完成自己的工作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 更重视可完成的合作过程，而不只看名次</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to a club disagreement</h2><p>Reply to Lin in Chinese. Answer whether you can join Wednesday’s discussion and whether you prefer interviews or a display. Explain your preference. Address the new restriction with a feasible alternative, and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. You may invent personal details. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小禾：我们要介绍学校的旧物再用活动。你周三午休能来讨论吗？你更想采访同学，还是做图片展示？现在老师说放学后不能再进教室，大家原来约好的时间不行了。请你想个办法，也告诉我还有什么需要确认。<br>小林</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can join Wednesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose interviews, a display or another relevant format.</li><li>Give a reason for your preference.</li><li>Offer a feasible way to work without after-school access.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>When an activity turned out differently</h2><p>Using the fictional activity card, write connected Chinese paragraphs for a classmate about an experience that changed your view. Include its time and context, at least two actions in sequence, the contrast between expectation and outcome, a reason or feeling, and one reflection or next step. You may add plausible details consistent with the card. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虚构活动卡<br>时间：上个月一个周六上午<br>地点：学校旧物再用活动<br>原先期待：担心不会修东西，觉得只能旁观<br>经过：先听老师介绍；帮助整理布袋；和同学一起修好松开的提手<br>结果：虽然不快，仍然帮助了别人<br>感受和下一步：自行选择，可表达仍有困难，但须与材料一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Saturday morning and the school reuse activity.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with what happened.</li><li>Explain a feeling or a reason.</li><li>State a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Discuss a goal and a change of plan</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate about a school project. Each file already contains two plays. Play it once, then allow 15 seconds to prepare and up to 30 seconds to respond. Link your opinion, an experience, an alternative and a next step. You may invent details. All four responses form one task /8; this is not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate are preparing a short introduction for a school activity. Personal experience may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State an opinion or need.</li><li>Use an experience to explain a reason.</li><li>Respond to a new condition with a feasible alternative.</li><li>Explain a final choice and next step.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Recommend a school action</h2><p>Recommend one of the two supplied plans to your class. Compare the plans, support your recommendation with two details from the card, identify one limitation, and give a practical next step. Either choice can receive full credit if its constraints are addressed. You have 60 seconds to prepare and up to 120 seconds to speak. Instructions are on screen, not a separate audio prompt.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班级情况：20人，周六上午有空，希望多数同学能参与；材料总预算50元。<br>甲：旧书分享，周六9:00–11:00，免费，每人带一本内容完整的书；图书角同时最多10人，可分批；需要2位同学整理推荐单。<br>乙：布袋修补，周六9:30–11:30，老师提供工具和补布，共需材料费30元；同时最多12人，本周只有这一场；学习者须带洗净的布袋。<br>可以推荐任一方案，但要说明怎样处理人数、准备或其他限制。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Give a first supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Give a different second supporting detail.</li><li>Identify a limitation of the recommended plan.</li><li>Propose a next step that addresses it.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>